{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Secret Valentine", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "One More Night Alone", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe events past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Inseparable Phrasal Verbs ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Phrasal verbs are two-part verbs consisting of a verb followed by an adverb particle (these look like prepositions, but do not have the same function in phrasal verbs). <br /> In some cases, it is not possible to separate the verb and the particle. These are called <span class=\"italic\">inseparable</span> phrasal verbs.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Phrasal Verbs  </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Meaning  </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" listen up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" listen carefully\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" taken aback\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to surprise\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" root for\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" support or cheer for\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" come about\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" turn into\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"become\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Hey Vanessa, <span class=\"strong\">listen up</span>! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How did that <span class=\"strong\">come about</span>?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Okay, I'm totally <span class=\"strong\">taken aback</span>!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Let's <span class=\"strong\">root for</span> V! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This has <span class=\"strong\">turned into </span>a great evening!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Modals for Suggestions, Necessity and Possibility", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Modals are auxiliary verbs that function in different ways. Modals  can offer suggestion, express necessity and show possibility.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " You use modals to talk about degrees of certainty, possibility and necessity.<br /><br /> You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. <br /><br /> Modals are used with the base form of the main verb. <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">Should</span> (modal) + <span class=\"italic\">go</span>(main verb)<br /> You can think of modals as \"helping verbs\". They add meaning to the main verb of a sentence.  <br /><br /> Modals talking about <span class=\"strong\">suggestions </span>are:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">can</span> and <span class=\"italic\">should</span>. <br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">Don't you think we <span class=\"strong\">should ask </span>Peter about his date? </span><br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">Maybe we <span class=\"strong\">should drop</span> the subject before anyone gets immensely uncomfortable.  </span><br /><br /> Modals talking about <span class=\"strong\">necessity </span> are: <br/><span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have to</span>, <span class=\"italic\">had better</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span>. <br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">have to respect</span> Peter's boundaries.</span> <br /><br /> Modals talking about <span class=\"strong\">possibility </span>are:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span> and <span class=\"italic\">might</span>. <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">We<span class=\"strong\"> might want </span>to relax and enjoy our evening together. </span><br /><br />  Note: '<span class=\"italic\">You shouldn't have!</span>' is a common phrase used when you receive a gift. It doesn't really mean you shouldn't have bought me a gift; it means you are thankful.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Don't you think we should ask Peter about his date?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Maybe we should drop the subject before anyone gets immensely uncomfortable. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We have to respect Peter's boundaries.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We might want to relax and enjoy our evening together.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You shouldn't have! ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to drop the subject", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stop talking about a subject", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Maybe we should drop the subject before anyone gets immensely uncomfortable. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are the words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "boundaries", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a limit that is traced to show the end and beginning of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have to respect Peter's boundaries.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "listen up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to listen carefully", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Hey Vanessa, listen up! I got Peter season tickets to see the Celtics!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to calm down ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to relax; to reduce anxiety", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Okay everyone, calm down.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "immensely ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to a great extent", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter is going to be immensely happy that we got tickets to Wednesday's game!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "public displays of affection", "type": "name"}, {"content": "physical affection shown in front of others", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On Valentine's day, however, there may be more public displays of affection than usual!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I describe people.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a story about falling in love.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use one or two inseparable phrasal verbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my story with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Tell a friend a story about two people you know who met and fell in love (your parents, aunt and uncle, friends etc.).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe each person and explain how they met. (Use phrasal verbs if possible.)", "type": "tex